WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.144 --> 00:00:14.455
That Mowgli stayed with Messua in her hut.

2
00:00:15.936 --> 00:00:19.459
As they ate dinner, she told him that her husband had died.

3
00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:23.242
"But you saved our lives that night, Mowgli."

4
00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:25.884
Her eyes filled with grateful tears.

5
00:00:25.904 --> 00:00:30.048
"And we have had a good life here.

6
00:00:30.872 --> 00:00:33.753
There's a village nearby, and I am content."

7
00:00:40.856 --> 00:00:43.257
In the morning Mowgli got ready to go.

8
00:00:43.277 --> 00:00:49.100
"Please visit again," Messua whispered, hugging him.

9
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.060
"I love you."

10
00:00:52.821 --> 00:00:54.382
Mowgli's throat felt tight.

11
00:00:54.402 --> 00:00:56.943
"I love you too, Messua.

12
00:00:57.923 --> 00:00:59.384
And I will come back soon.

13
00:01:00.072 --> 00:01:00.892
I promise."

14
00:01:03.753 --> 00:01:08.214
As he headed toward the marsh, a large beast jumped out of the tall grass.

15
00:01:09.755 --> 00:01:12.496
"Bagheera!" Mowgli said in surprise.

16
00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:14.616
"What are you doing here?"

17
00:01:14.636 --> 00:01:18.297
"I followed you," Bagheera replied.

18
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:23.379
"Again?" Mowgli laughed and shook his head.

19
00:01:25.059 --> 00:01:26.840
"You're always following me.

20
00:01:27.728 --> 00:01:30.049
So are Mother Wolf and Gray Brother."

21
00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:32.429
Bagheera looked nervous.

22
00:01:32.449 --> 00:01:36.550
"Are you Are you coming back to the jungle?"

23
00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:37.411
he asked.

24
00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:41.072
"I I thought you might stay here with the woman."

25
00:01:42.272 --> 00:01:43.372
Mowgli shook his head.

26
00:01:43.392 --> 00:01:47.333
"I don't think I belong with people, Bagheera.

27
00:01:49.514 --> 00:01:52.014
The man pack threw me out—remember?

28
00:01:52.615 --> 00:01:54.075
Just like the wolf pack."

29
00:01:55.235 --> 00:01:57.376
Bagheera studied Mowgli for a second.

30
00:01:59.164 --> 00:02:00.465
Then he lifted his chin.

31
00:02:00.485 --> 00:02:02.626
"Feel under my jaw."

32
00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:08.649
Mowgli obediently put his fingers under Bagheera's silky chin.

33
00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.791
The panther's fur covered thick muscles.

34
00:02:13.172 --> 00:02:15.553
Then Mowgli touched a bare patch.

35
00:02:15.573 --> 00:02:17.334
"What's this?"

36
00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:18.394
he asked.

37
00:02:18.414 --> 00:02:21.916
"It is the mark of a collar," Bagheera said.

38
00:02:21.936 --> 00:02:28.700
"No one in the jungle knows this—I was also born among people, Mowgli.

39
00:02:31.297 --> 00:02:33.197
I lived in a cage at the king's palace."

40
00:02:33.217 --> 00:02:37.059
"What?" Mowgli blinked in surprise.

41
00:02:38.119 --> 00:02:40.400
Bagheera had lived with humans too?

42
00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:46.361
"That's why I spoke for you at the council when you were a little cub," Bagheera went on.

43
00:02:48.202 --> 00:02:50.683
"My mother died in the cages at the palace.

44
00:02:51.463 --> 00:03:00.331
After that, I had no family there, and Mowgli couldn't imagine the beautiful, strong panther trapped in a

45
00:03:00.392 --> 00:03:04.074
cage. "The cage must have felt like prison."

46
00:03:04.094 --> 00:03:07.797
"It was a prison," Bagheera said.

47
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:12.061
"I lived there without ever seeing the jungle.

48
00:03:13.322 --> 00:03:16.484
Then one night I mysteriously found my strength.

49
00:03:17.785 --> 00:03:21.668
I told myself I was a panther—not a plaything for people.

50
00:03:22.909 --> 00:03:25.932
And I broke the silly lock with one blow of my paw."

51
00:03:27.044 --> 00:03:28.045
Mowgli grinned.

52
00:03:28.866 --> 00:03:31.508
That was something he could picture Bagheera doing.

53
00:03:31.528 --> 00:03:34.691
"Now you know my secret, Little Brother.

54
00:03:35.771 --> 00:03:37.913
I returned to the jungle where I belonged.

55
00:03:38.974 --> 00:03:41.176
As for you Bagheera paused.

56
00:03:42.857 --> 00:03:43.738
"You are a human.

57
00:03:44.699 --> 00:03:48.002
So one day you too will return to where you belong."

58
00:03:49.503 --> 00:03:52.005
"Nope. Sorry, Bagheera, but you're wrong."

59
00:03:52.605 --> 00:03:54.407
Mowgli shook his head firmly.

60
00:03:54.427 --> 00:03:57.489
"I won't ever live with people again.

61
00:03:58.329 --> 00:04:00.390
I'll visit Messua, but that's about it."

62
00:04:04.872 --> 00:04:06.052
He patted the panther.

63
00:04:06.072 --> 00:04:13.476
"And when I'm older and on my own, I'll come back to visit you and Baloo—" Just then

64
00:04:13.996 --> 00:04:17.477
a girl in a flowing white dress appeared on the path.

65
00:04:18.738 --> 00:04:21.079
Mowgli and Bagheera ducked behind some bushes.

66
00:04:22.559 --> 00:04:26.285
As the girl passed, Mowgli moved the bushes with his hand.

67
00:04:27.365 --> 00:04:29.506
He watched the girl walk toward the marsh.

68
00:04:34.989 --> 00:04:39.851
boy is both man and wolf," Bagheera thought, watching him tenderly.

69
00:04:39.871 --> 00:04:43.832
"But one day he will become more man than wolf."

70
00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:50.135
The girl disappeared, and Bagheera nudged Mowgli with his nose.

71
00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:52.936
"Ready to go home, Little Brother?"

72
00:04:54.768 --> 00:04:58.454
"Yes." Mowgli leaped onto the panther's back.

73
00:04:59.255 --> 00:05:02.419
Then together they went back into the jungle.
